#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:55
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:57
msgid ""
"Suppose you want to write real-time safe code, and you've heard about the "
"many dangers of calling ``new`` during the real-time critical section, "
"because the default heap allocator on most platforms is nondeterministic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:59
msgid ""
"By default, many C++ standard library structures will implicitly allocate "
"memory as they grow, such as ``std::vector``. However, these data structures "
"also accept an \"Allocator\" template argument. If you specify a custom "
"allocator to one of these data structures, it will use that allocator "
"instead of the system allocator to grow or shrink the data structure. Your "
"custom allocator could have a pool of memory preallocated on the stack, "
"which might be better suited to real-time applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:64
msgid ""
"In the ROS 2 C++ client library (rclcpp), we are following a similar "
"philosophy to the C++ standard library. Publishers, subscribers, and the "
"Executor accept an Allocator template parameter that controls allocations "
"made by that entity during execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:68
msgid "Writing an allocator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:70
msgid ""
"To write an allocator compatible with ROS 2's allocator interface, your "
"allocator must be compatible with the C++ standard library allocator "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:72
msgid ""
"Since C++17, the standard library provides something called "
"``std::pmr::memory_resource``. This is a class that can be derived from to "
"create a custom allocator that fulfills a minimum set of requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:75
msgid ""
"For example, the following declaration for a custom memory resource fulfills "
"the requirements (of course, you would still need to implement the declared "
"functions in this class):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:77
msgid ""
"class CustomMemoryResource : public std::pmr::memory_resource\n"
"{\n"
"private:\n"
"  void * do_allocate(std::size_t bytes, std::size_t alignment) override;\n"
"\n"
"  void do_deallocate(\n"
"    void * p, std::size_t bytes,\n"
"    std::size_t alignment) override;\n"
"\n"
"  bool do_is_equal(\n"
"    const std::pmr::memory_resource & other) const noexcept override;\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:92
msgid ""
"To learn about the full capabilities of ``std::pmr::memory_resource``, see "
"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:95
msgid "Providing an allocator for rcl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:97
msgid ""
"rclcpp is built on top of the C library rcl, and rclcpp uses rcl to allocate "
"memory for the publishers and subscriptions it creates. To route those "
"allocations to a custom allocator, rclcpp needs a C-style "
"``rcl_allocator_t``,  and a set of ``allocate``, ``deallocate``, "
"``reallocate`` and ``zero_allocate`` callbacks. Your allocator provides "
"these capabilities through a ``get_rcl_allocator()`` member function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:101
msgid ""
"The callbacks cannot simply forward to the C++ allocator for a number of "
"reasons. For example, rcl's ``deallocate`` does not pass the size of the "
"memory block, but ``std::pmr::memory_resource::deallocate`` must receive the "
"size and alignment that were used to allocate it. The  callbacks are called "
"from C code, so they cannot use  C++ ``throw:`` semantics, instead they must "
"return ``nullptr`` on failure in a manner similar to those used by  "
"``malloc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:105
msgid ""
"For ``std::pmr``, a small wrapper around ``std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator`` "
"can store the size of each block in a header in front of it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:107
msgid ""
"#include <cstring>\n"
"#include <limits>\n"
"#include <memory_resource>\n"
"\n"
"#include \"rcl/allocator.h\"\n"
"\n"
"template<typename T = void>\n"
"struct PmrAllocator : std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>\n"
"{\n"
"  using std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::polymorphic_allocator;\n"
"\n"
"  // Share the memory resource when changing the allocator's element type.\n"
"  template<typename U>\n"
"  PmrAllocator(const PmrAllocator<U> & other) noexcept\n"
"  : std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>(other.resource()) {}\n"
"\n"
"  // Let allocator traits create this wrapper for another element type.\n"
"  template<typename U>\n"
"  struct rebind\n"
"  {\n"
"    using other = PmrAllocator<U>;\n"
"  };\n"
"\n"
"  rcl_allocator_t get_rcl_allocator() const\n"
"  {\n"
"    // Connect the C callbacks to the same memory resource as the C++ "
"allocator.\n"
"    rcl_allocator_t rcl_allocator = rcl_get_default_allocator();\n"
"    rcl_allocator.allocate = &allocate_block;\n"
"    rcl_allocator.deallocate = &deallocate_block;\n"
"    rcl_allocator.reallocate = &reallocate_block;\n"
"    rcl_allocator.zero_allocate = &zero_allocate_block;\n"
"    // rcl passes this state pointer to each callback.\n"
"    rcl_allocator.state = this->resource();\n"
"    return rcl_allocator;\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"private:\n"
"  // Reserve space before each payload for its size, keeping the payload "
"aligned.\n"
"  static constexpr size_t header = alignof(std::max_align_t);\n"
"\n"
"  static void * allocate_block(size_t size, void * state) noexcept\n"
"  {\n"
"    // Check that adding the header will not overflow the allocation size.\n"
"    if (size > (std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max)() - header) {\n"
"      return nullptr;\n"
"    }\n"
"    try {\n"
"      auto resource = static_cast<std::pmr::memory_resource *>(state);\n"
"      auto base = static_cast<char *>(resource->allocate(header + size, "
"header));\n"
"      // Save the size in the header and return only the payload to rcl.\n"
"      std::memcpy(base, &size, sizeof(size));\n"
"      return base + header;\n"
"    } catch (...) {\n"
"      // C callers expect nullptr on allocation failure, not a C++ "
"exception.\n"
"      return nullptr;\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  static void deallocate_block(void * pointer, void * state) noexcept\n"
"  {\n"
"    if (pointer == nullptr) {\n"
"      return;\n"
"    }\n"
"    // rcl supplies no size, so recover it from the header before the "
"payload.\n"
"    auto base = static_cast<char *>(pointer) - header;\n"
"    size_t size;\n"
"    std::memcpy(&size, base, sizeof(size));\n"
"    // The resource requires the original address, total size, and "
"alignment.\n"
"    static_cast<std::pmr::memory_resource *>(state)->deallocate(base, header "
"+ size, header);\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  static void * reallocate_block(void * pointer, size_t size, void * state) "
"noexcept\n"
"  {\n"
"    // Allocate first so a failure leaves the original block untouched.\n"
"    void * new_pointer = allocate_block(size, state);\n"
"    if (new_pointer == nullptr) {\n"
"      return nullptr;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (pointer != nullptr) {\n"
"      size_t old_size;\n"
"      std::memcpy(&old_size, static_cast<char *>(pointer) - header, "
"sizeof(old_size));\n"
"      // Copy only what fits, then release the original block.\n"
"      std::memcpy(new_pointer, pointer, old_size < size ? old_size : size);\n"
"      deallocate_block(pointer, state);\n"
"    }\n"
"    return new_pointer;\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  static void * zero_allocate_block(size_t count, size_t size, void * state) "
"noexcept\n"
"  {\n"
"    // Check for multiplication overflow before allocating the array.\n"
"    if (size != 0 && count > (std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max)() / size) {\n"
"      return nullptr;\n"
"    }\n"
"    void * pointer = allocate_block(count * size, state);\n"
"    if (pointer != nullptr) {\n"
"      std::memset(pointer, 0, count * size);\n"
"    }\n"
"    return pointer;\n"
"  }\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:211
msgid ""
"If your allocator already has C-style functions that do not need the size, "
"its ``get_rcl_allocator()`` can forward to them directly. The TLSF allocator "
"described at the end of this tutorial demonstrates how to do this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:214
msgid ""
"The full implementation of the custom allocator for this tutorial is in "
"https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_cpp/src/topics/"
"allocator_tutorial_pmr.cpp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:217
msgid "Writing an example main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:219
msgid ""
"Once you have written a valid C++ allocator, you must pass it as a shared "
"pointer to your publisher, subscriber, and executor. But first, we'll "
"declare a few aliases to shorten the names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:222
msgid ""
"using Alloc = PmrAllocator<void>;\n"
"using MessageAllocTraits =\n"
"  rclcpp::allocator::AllocRebind<std_msgs::msg::UInt32, Alloc>;\n"
"using MessageAlloc = MessageAllocTraits::allocator_type;\n"
"using MessageDeleter = rclcpp::allocator::Deleter<MessageAlloc, "
"std_msgs::msg::UInt32>;\n"
"using MessageUniquePtr = std::unique_ptr<std_msgs::msg::UInt32, "
"MessageDeleter>;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:231
msgid "Now we can create our resources with the custom allocator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:233
msgid ""
"CustomMemoryResource mem_resource{};\n"
"auto alloc = std::make_shared<Alloc>(&mem_resource);\n"
"rclcpp::PublisherOptionsWithAllocator<Alloc> publisher_options;\n"
"publisher_options.allocator = alloc;\n"
"auto publisher = node->create_publisher<std_msgs::msg::UInt32>(\n"
"  \"allocator_tutorial\", 10, publisher_options);\n"
"\n"
"rclcpp::SubscriptionOptionsWithAllocator<Alloc> subscription_options;\n"
"subscription_options.allocator = alloc;\n"
"auto msg_mem_strat = std::make_shared<\n"
"  rclcpp::message_memory_strategy::MessageMemoryStrategy<\n"
"    std_msgs::msg::UInt32, Alloc>>(alloc);\n"
"auto subscriber = node->create_subscription<std_msgs::msg::UInt32>(\n"
"  \"allocator_tutorial\", 10, callback, subscription_options, "
"msg_mem_strat);\n"
"\n"
"rclcpp::ExecutorOptions options;\n"
"rclcpp::executors::SingleThreadedExecutor executor(options);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:253
msgid ""
"You must also instantiate a custom deleter and allocator for use when "
"allocating messages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:255
msgid ""
"MessageDeleter message_deleter;\n"
"MessageAlloc message_alloc = *alloc;\n"
"rclcpp::allocator::set_allocator_for_deleter(&message_deleter, "
"&message_alloc);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:261
msgid ""
"Once you've add the node to the executor, it is time to spin. We'll use the "
"custom allocator to allocate each message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:264
msgid ""
"uint32_t i = 0;\n"
"while (rclcpp::ok()) {\n"
"  auto ptr = MessageAllocTraits::allocate(message_alloc, 1);\n"
"  MessageAllocTraits::construct(message_alloc, ptr);\n"
"  MessageUniquePtr msg(ptr, message_deleter);\n"
"  msg->data = i;\n"
"  ++i;\n"
"  publisher->publish(std::move(msg));\n"
"  rclcpp::sleep_for(10ms);\n"
"  executor.spin_some();\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:279
msgid "Passing an allocator to the intra-process pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:281
msgid ""
"Even though we instantiated a publisher and subscriber in the same process, "
"we aren't using the intra-process pipeline yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:283
msgid ""
"The IntraProcessManager is a class that is usually hidden from the user, but "
"in order to pass a custom allocator to it we need to expose it by getting it "
"from the rclcpp Context. The IntraProcessManager makes use of several "
"standard library structures, so without a custom allocator it will call the "
"default ``new``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:286
msgid ""
"auto context = rclcpp::contexts::get_global_default_context();\n"
"auto options = rclcpp::NodeOptions()\n"
"  .context(context)\n"
"  .use_intra_process_comms(true);\n"
"auto node = rclcpp::Node::make_shared(\"allocator_example\", options);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:294
msgid ""
"Make sure to instantiate publishers and subscribers AFTER constructing the "
"node in this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:297
msgid "Testing and verifying the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:299
msgid "How do you know that your custom allocator is actually getting called?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:301
msgid ""
"The obvious thing to do would be to count the calls made to your custom "
"allocator's ``allocate`` and ``deallocate`` functions and compare that to "
"the calls to ``new`` and ``delete``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:303
msgid "Adding counting to the custom allocator is easy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:305
msgid ""
"void * do_allocate(std::size_t size, std::size_t alignment) override\n"
"{\n"
"  // ...\n"
"  num_allocs++;\n"
"  // ...\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"void do_deallocate(\n"
"  void * p, std::size_t bytes,\n"
"  std::size_t alignment) override\n"
"{\n"
"  // ...\n"
"  num_deallocs++;\n"
"  // ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:323
msgid "You can also override the global ``new`` and ``delete`` operators:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:325
msgid ""
"void * operator new(std::size_t size)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (is_running) {\n"
"    global_runtime_allocs++;\n"
"  }\n"
"  return std::malloc(size);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"void operator delete(void * ptr, size_t) noexcept\n"
"{\n"
"  if (ptr != nullptr) {\n"
"    if (is_running) {\n"
"      global_runtime_deallocs++;\n"
"    }\n"
"    std::free(ptr);\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"void operator delete(void * ptr) noexcept\n"
"{\n"
"  if (ptr != nullptr) {\n"
"    if (is_running) {\n"
"      global_runtime_deallocs++;\n"
"    }\n"
"    std::free(ptr);\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Allocator-Template-Tutorial.rst:355
msgid ""
"where the variables we are incrementing are just global static integers, and "
"``is_running`` is a global static boolean that gets toggled right before the "
"call to ``spin``."
msgstr ""

